<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H2140</pnldref><english><title>Custody/control of a thing knowing it was a counterfeit protected coin with intent - Forgery and Counterfeiting Act 1981</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>custody</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>control</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>counterfeiting</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>counterfeited</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>pass</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>passed</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>passing</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tender</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tendered</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tendering</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>deliver</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>delivered</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>delivering</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..) had in your custody or under your control a thing which was and which you knew or believed to be a counterfeit of a protected coin, namely **(..SPECIFY DETAILS..), intending to &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(A)_[pass or tender it as genuine]_&lt;br /&gt;(B)_[deliver it to another with the intent that the other or another should pass or tender it as genuine]_</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to sections 16(1) and 22 of the Forgery and Counterfeiting Act 1981.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt; had custody/control of thing which was and knew/believed thing to be counterfeit protected coin &lt;br /&gt; intending to pass or tender it as genuine/deliver it to another to pass or tender it as genuine</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code></code><description>Criminal lifestyle offence under Schedule 2 to POCA - consider confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) Section 16(3) provides that it is immaterial that a coin is not in a fit state to be tendered or the making or counterfeiting of it finished or perfected.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) See also offence wording H2121.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><descr